# SRG-APP-000830-WSR-000190  -  CAT II
# The web server must, for password-based authentication, maintain a list of
# commonly used, expected, or compromised passwords on an
# organization-defined frequency.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000830-WSR-000190
group:           V-264345
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   ORGANIZATIONAL
grade:           D
decidable:       manual
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-004058
control_rev5:    IA-5

contribution:    None toward the list itself, and the web tier adds nothing beyond the
                 platform: Splunk Web keeps no credential store of its own and
                 authenticates through authentication.conf, which has no setting holding or
                 referencing a list of commonly used, expected, or compromised passwords.
                 The product's only weak-password controls are the composition and history
                 settings in [splunk_auth], assessed under SRG-APP-000845 and
                 SRG-APP-000870.

external:        The list and its maintenance frequency - carried by organizational policy.
external:        Screening of passwords against the list at the point of authentication -
                 carried by the directory service or identity provider where authType is
                 LDAP, SAML, or ProxySSO.
external:        Where a reverse proxy or SSO proxy fronts Splunk Web, any deny-list
                 screening at that tier is carried by that component.

manual_reason:   No conf key in the product expresses a password deny list or its
                 maintenance frequency, so no observed configuration value can decide this
                 requirement.

citation:        splunk-spec-files/authentication.conf.spec:437-600;
                 splunk-spec-files/web.conf.spec:16 ([settings] holds no credential or
                 password-list setting)
finding:         Not a finding against the application: the web tier authenticates through
                 authentication.conf, which has no password deny-list setting, so this
                 requirement is carried by organizational policy and by the identity
                 provider that screens passwords; this determination is from the
                 perspective of the application layer alone.
